From 6aa1a226525922c3f6b4a60c103c0e0d28f748d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:20:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ac/qt: "Connect as a Nintendo Zone hotspot" option

The 3DS recognises a Nintendo Zone by the access point: an open network
named "NintendoSpotPass1" is the EUR Nintendo Zone hotspot in the system's
hotspot list (3dbrew "Nintendo Zone"; also how SatellaZone's readme makes
the EUR Nintendo Zone app appear). Tangelo's virtual access point is
called "Tangelo", so games that only handed out gifts at a Nintendo Zone
(e.g. Animal Crossing: New Leaf at the post office) refuse.

New checkbox in Configure > General > Network > SpotPass, "Connect as a
Nintendo Zone hotspot" (setting nintendo_zone_mode, off by default).
When on:
- GetCurrentAPInfo reports SSID "NintendoSpotPass1";
- GetNZoneApNumService fills in an ApNum and service name (placeholders;
  the real values came from Nintendo's hotspot list);
- GetConnectingLocation reports 1 (assumed to mean Nintendo Zone) unless
  the hidden ac_connecting_location setting overrides it.
When off, everything behaves as before.

